  - brevity principle
  - machine-generated text detection
  - quantitative linguistics
  - Spanish
abstract: >-
  Replication materials (Python code, result tables and figures) for the article
  "Las leyes estadísticas del lenguaje como marcador de estilo para la detección
  de textos robóticos en español". Fifteen vocabulary-independent stylometric
  features derived from Zipf's law, Heaps' law and the brevity principle are used
  to distinguish human-authored Spanish scientific articles from those generated
  by six LLMs, on a paired panel of 90 articles × 7 authors from the ROBOT-TALK corpus.
